From a8d116f1f538b54de7d0efd520e62c58d6eca451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Feb 2024 21:54:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: hisilicon: add support for PLL

Several HiSilicon SoCs need a shared PLL clock type. Add the PLL ops and
a bulk registrar declared in clk.h; the dividers are read when the clock
is registered because the clock core computes a rate and may run
determine_rate() before prepare(), the rate math carries its
multiply-accumulate in a u64 and takes the remainder through the div64
helpers so it compiles and links on arm, and the hi3559a file-local
registrar gives up the name hisi_clk_register_pll to the new generic one
so the static does not collide with the header declaration. This is a
preparation step for the SoC drivers that publish PLL cells.

Signed-off-by: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/Makefile      |   2 +-
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk-hi3559a.c |  10 +-
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk-pll.c     | 195 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk.c         |  24 ++++
 drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk.h         |  12 ++
 5 files changed, 238 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk-pll.c

